  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Phillips 66 recorded $582M in federal contract obligations for FY26 to date. Phillips 66 received 460 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.3M. Obligations are down 9.1% year over year. Historical annual obligations show a rise from $329M in FY21 to $640M in FY25, with FY26 at $582M through the current reporting period. The mix of award count and average award size suggests Phillips 66 wins many mid-sized contracts rather than a few very large single awards. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations. Contractors and agencies tracking Phillips 66 should note the recent year-over-year decline in obligations while viewing the FY26 total in the context of the multi-year trend that peaked at $640M in FY25.",
